{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Isaac breathed his last.</b> There is no earlier and later in the Torah. The sale of Joseph preceded the death of Isaac by twelve years. For when Jacob was born, Isaac was sixty years old, as it is said: ״וְיִצְחָק בֶּן שִׁשִּׁים שָׁנָה״ and so forth. And Isaac died in the year 120 of Jacob's life — if you subtract sixty from one hundred and eighty, there remain 120. And Joseph was sold at seventeen years old, and that year was the year 108 of Jacob's life. How so? At sixty-three he received the blessing; fourteen years he was hidden in the academy of Shem and Ever — that is seventy-seven; and fourteen years he served for a wife, and at the end of the fourteen Joseph was born, as it is said: ״וַיְהִי כַּאֲשֶׁר יָלְדָה רָחֵל אֶת יוֹסֵף״ and so forth — that is ninety-one; and seventeen more until Joseph was sold — that is one hundred and eight. (It is further spelled out from Scripture: from when Joseph was sold until Jacob came to Egypt was twenty-two years, as it is said: ״וְיוֹסֵף בֶּן שְׁלֹשִׁים שָׁנָה״ and so forth, and seven years of plenty and two years of famine — that is twenty-two; and it is written: ״יְמֵי שְׁנֵי מְגוּרַי שְׁלֹשִׁים וּמְאַת שָׁנָה״ — so Jacob at the time of the sale was 108.)"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:16.666204573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}